# vulnpipe: how the implementation works

This file explains the `vulnpipe` package end to end: what each stage does,
which command runs it, which file it writes, and where the numbers in the
thesis come from. It was written from the code (October 2026); where the
notes in `docs/` disagree, trust the code and this file.

## 1. What the project does

`vulnpipe` compares three families of vulnerability detectors on Java code
for two CWEs, CWE-89 (SQL Injection) and CWE-22 (Path Traversal):

1. **SAST**: Semgrep (taint mode, custom rules) and PMD (built-in rules and
   custom syntactic XPath rules), run in pinned Docker images.
2. **LLMs**: local models served by Ollama, asked "is this code vulnerable?"
   with a JSON answer format.
3. **Hybrid**: SAST produces candidate alerts, and an LLM acts as a
   *confirmer* that keeps or rejects each alert.

Every detector is forced into the same output record (a `Finding` with a
binary `verdict` per snippet), so one metrics stage can score all of them
against the same ground truth (`Snippet.label`). The main corpus is OWASP
Benchmark v1.2 (772 servlet files); Juliet is a secondary/control corpus.

```
                     data/owasp-benchmark (sparse git clone)
                     expectedresults-1.2.csv + BenchmarkTest*.java
                                   |
                     vulnpipe corpus build --only owasp
                     (corpus/owasp.py: filter sqli+pathtraver,
                      neutralise(): strip comments, rename test, ...)
                                   |
                                   v
                          corpus/owasp.jsonl   (772 Snippets, ground truth)
                                   |
        +--------------------------+---------------------------+
        |                          |                           |
  vulnpipe sast run           vulnpipe llm run                 |
  (materialize .java,         (prompt per snippet,             |
   docker PMD / Semgrep,       Ollama, parse JSON)             |
   SARIF -> Issues ->          |                               |
   1 Finding per snippet)      |                               |
        |                          v                           |
        |              <model>__<strategy>_perSnippet.jsonl     |
        v                     llm_runs/<tool>_runs.jsonl        |
  semgrep_perSnippet.jsonl                                     |
  pmd-{vanilla,custom}_perSnippet.jsonl                        |
  scan/semgrep_traces.txt  (text pass with --dataflow-traces)  |
        |                                                      |
        +------> vulnpipe hybrid run --sast ... [--traces] <----+
                 (candidates = SAST verdict 1 -> LLM confirm/reject;
                  non-candidates: safe (reject) or zero-shot (augment))
                                   |
                                   v
                 hybrid__<sast>__<model>__<scope>[__trace|__trace-hints]_perSnippet.jsonl
                                   |
        all *_perSnippet.jsonl ----+
                                   v
                 vulnpipe metrics --findings ... [--compare SAST LLM HYB]
                 -> metrics/owasp/per_tool.csv  (P, R, FPR, F1, CI, TP/FP/TN/FN)
                 -> stdout: HIS + McNemar
                                   |
                                   v
                 vulnpipe figures ...  /  scripts/thesis_figures.py

  side path: scripts/pilot.py (60 Semgrep alerts, Youden J) to pick the
